  "title": "Benchmarking Opus 4.6 For Vuln Detection: Flashes Of Brilliance But Lots of Noise",
  "summary": "We tested Opus 4.6 against 435 known vulnerable C functions from real CVEs. With good prompting and tools, it found up to 28.5% of vulnerabilities — impressive compared to human review, but with high false positive rates and inconsistency that underline the need for more sophisticated systems.",
